# project.yml.example — how to set your signing identity
#
# project.yml is committed with a placeholder Team ID so no personal identifier
# lives in the repo. To build, put YOUR Apple Developer / Personal Team ID into
# project.yml without committing it:
#
#   1. Find your Team ID:
#        Xcode → Settings → Accounts → select your Apple ID → "Manage Certificates"
#        (or the 10-char ID shown next to the team), e.g. ABCDE12345
#      Or from the CLI:
#        security find-identity -v -p codesigning   # the "(TEAMID)" in the name
#
#   2. Set it in project.yml:
#        settings.base.DEVELOPMENT_TEAM: "ABCDE12345"
#
#   3. Keep your local edit out of git so the ID is never committed:
#        git update-index --skip-worktree project.yml
#      (undo later with: git update-index --no-skip-worktree project.yml)
#
# Note: the Team ID is NOT a secret — it ships inside every signed app binary —
# but it's a personal identifier, so it's kept out of the public repo by choice.
#
# The same applies to ExportOptions.plist (teamID) — see ExportOptions.plist.example.
